## 2. Senior UI/UX & Graphic Design System Standards (Modern & Interactive)

Every interface generated must look modern, sleek, polished, and highly engaging—designed like a Senior UI/UX Graphic Designer built it. Avoid plain, unstyled layouts or generic Bootstrap-looking Tailwind blocks.

### Aesthetics & Visual Polish

- **Modern Color Palettes & Depth:** Use rich, deliberate color systems with slate/zinc neutral tones (`bg-slate-900`, `bg-slate-50`, `text-slate-900`). Incorporate glassmorphism overlays (`backdrop-blur-md bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/70`), subtle ambient glows (`shadow-indigo-500/10`), and delicate borders (`border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80`).
- **Typography & Scale:** Enforce strong typographic hierarchy with variable font weights (`font-semibold`, `tracking-tight`), crisp contrast, and balanced line heights (`leading-relaxed`). Use subtext with muted opacity (`text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400`).
- **Spatial Grid & Geometry:** Use consistent spacing scales (`p-4`, `p-6`, `gap-4`, `gap-6`), soft corner radii (`rounded-xl`, `rounded-2xl`), and balanced card grid structures.

### Interactive Micro-Interactions & Motion

- **Fluid State Transitions:** Apply smooth transition curves (`transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out` or `duration-300`) to interactive elements.
- **Tactile Feedback:** Buttons and interactive cards must feel physical—use dynamic hover translation (`hover:-translate-y-0.5`), active press states (`active:translate-y-0 active:scale-[0.98]`), and elevation shifts (`hover:shadow-lg hover:shadow-indigo-500/10`).
- **Interactive Skeleton States:** Loading states must use animated pulse skeletons (`animate-pulse bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 rounded-lg`) rather than plain text spinners whenever content is fetching.
- **Dark Mode Support:** All components must natively support seamless light and dark mode modes via Tailwind `dark:` variants.

