## 3. Per-Feature Module Structure

Align with enterprise SPA rules. When introducing a new domain or module, organize files logically in dedicated module paths:

- `app/Services/ModuleNameService.php`
- `app/Repositories/ModuleNameRepository.php`
- `app/Http/Controllers/API/ModuleNameController.php`
- `resources/js/modules/module-name.js`
- New functions and module components live in their **own directory/folder** when introducing a new feature.

---

## 4. Reuse Before Inventing

Before writing new code, check for existing components, services, or helpers to extend or reuse:

- **Backend:** Reuse Services, Traits, and Helpers in `app/Services`, `app/Traits` — eliminate duplicated controller logic.
- **Validation:** Utilize shared `FormRequest` classes or custom validation `Rules`.
- **API Standard Response:** Enforce a consistent API response format via a standard helper or trait: `{ status, message, data|errors }`.
- **Blade UI:** Reuse UI Blade components (`<x-button>`, `<x-card>`, `<x-input>`, `<x-modal>`, `<x-table>`).
- **JavaScript:** Utilize shared modules in `resources/js/utils` (or equivalent). Axios handles all API requests — avoid full-page reloads.
- **CSS:** Use Tailwind CSS exclusively via the global `resources/css/app.css`. Use `@apply` or theme design tokens for repeated patterns — never create page-specific CSS files or duplicate utility dumps.
- **DataTables:** Every listing/management table must use `resources/js/utils/datatable/` (`createApicsDataTable`) per `.cursor/rules/global-datatable-standards.mdc` — search, filters, export, responsive child rows, sticky **icon-only** Actions (`⋮`, no text on the trigger), right-click menu, toast + confirm. Do not hand-roll static `<tbody>` lists or labeled action buttons in cells.

